      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofcedarbluff.com/about",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on the historic Old Kentucky Turnpike, a street unchanged since its 1848 charter, stretching from a restored grist mill to a 1873 governor’s birthplace.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedar_Bluff%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Jones Chapel Cemetery in Cedar Bluff holds graves of Civil War soldiers from both sides, reminding drivers of the town’s wartime history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cedar_bluff_virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Clinch Valley Blanket Mill, operating from 1890 through World War II, produced Goodwin weavers’ cloth in Cedar Bluff.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedar_Bluff%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Virginia’s Civil War Trails program marks two battle sites in Cedar Bluff, highlighting the town’s role in Confederate defenses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cedar_bluff_virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Cedar Bluff Overlook Park sits high on a bluff overlooking the Clinch River, offering interpretive signs about endangered species and geology.",
